## Overview

The app crashes while a user is editing a product&#39;s price in the product listing screen. After the app validates the entered price against the server (an &quot;absurd price check&quot;), the success callback tries to insert a value into an array at an invalid position — causing a fatal Swift crash. This affects sellers who update product prices and can reproduce whenever the price validation API returns a response while the product list UI is in a specific state.

[View in Firebase Crashlytics →](https://console.firebase.google.com/u/0/project/artful-affinity-634/crashlytics/app/ios:com.indiamart.m/issues/9ff722bf29d21fa584f4e1082185c8ed?time=30d&types=crash&sessionEventKey=ba39e084ec6e44ccb356618f6fff8266_2193933769402963992)

## Relevant Code / Files Involved

